# Phase discipline

Read [docs/master-spec.md](docs/master-spec.md) and the current V1 item in [docs/roadmap.md](docs/roadmap.md) before changing code.

Work only on the current V1 item. Phase 1 through Phase 11 are complete. See [docs/phase-11.md](docs/phase-11.md). Fly.io is accepted ([docs/phase-fly.md](docs/phase-fly.md)). Hyperliquid and copy leftover desk-test wait for V1 system test. Do not start a later V1 item or any V2 item until Click asks.

Feature work happens on `develop`. Merge to `main` only when the user is ready for production.

Phase 11 is the first managing playbook. Type `dca` on the desk. Same `futures_*` ledger and `runFuturesCommand`. The app owns orders and exits. Signals only arm. Stacked playbooks, one per contract and side. The engine worker claims **one desk at a time** (Postgres leases). Do not call private exchange APIs from the browser. Paper accounts still use the in-app ledger.

**Current V1 item: UI refinement and cleanup** (V1 item 3). Identity and 2FA are accepted. Started 17 Sep 2026. Work only what Click asks on this item. Next after that is entitlements / plan gates, then onboarding. V2 (webhooks, backup candles, scale-in, MEXC, admin roles, …) has no order.

Do not create later-phase tables or speculative architecture. Standing notes: [docs/click-list.md](docs/click-list.md).

Keep dependencies minimal. Prefer the simplest solution that satisfies the current phase.

Stop at the end of the item. After acceptance criteria pass, report results and wait for instruction.
